{
  "requirement": "The mdBook preprocessor MUST report an error when a generated evidence detail page would use the path of an existing book chapter.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Implementation.** `DetailPlan::find` in `src/index.rs` (lines 261–316) carries the `{impl}` markers for this requirement, one on the function and one on the check itself.\n- It computes each generated page path with `detail_path`: the defining chapter's path without its extension, joined with `<name>.md`.\n- It collects the paths of every existing book chapter, `existing_paths`, from `book.chapters()`.\n- It returns `invalid_index(\"generated evidence page … conflicts with a book chapter\")` whenever a generated path is in `existing_paths`.\n- `preprocess_book` in `src/lib.rs` calls `DetailPlan::find(...)?` before `populate`, so the error stops the preprocessor before any book mutation. `populate` is the step that adds pages.\n- The check runs whether or not an index directive exists, because it covers every definition's detail page. That matches the requirement, which is not limited to the index.\n- I found no other code that implements part of this requirement, so no marking gap.\n\n**Test.** `generated_detail_path_cannot_replace_a_chapter` (`src/index.rs`, lines 1410–1440) is marked `{test}`.\n- It builds a book with an existing chapter at `requirements/requirements.ready.md`.\n- It defines `requirements.ready` in `requirements.md`. The generated path is therefore `requirements/requirements.ready.md`, which collides with that chapter.\n- It asserts that `find` returns an error containing \"conflicts with a book chapter\".\n- Non-conflicting cases are exercised by the success-path tests, for example `index_shows_evidence_states_and_links_generated_chapters`. These show that normal generation produces no error.\n\n**Minor observation, not a blocker.** The same loop also rejects two generated pages that share a path (`!generated.insert(path)`). The requirement does not specify this, and no test covers it. It looks unreachable in practice: full definition names are deduplicated, so each generated path is unique. It is defensive code that sits under the same `{impl}` marker. Its error message is slightly imprecise for that case, but it does not alter the specified behavior.\n\nThe obligation is implemented and tested.",
